phy: tegra: xusb-tegra210: power on USB 3 lanes named "xusb"

Under 5.10 the onboard hub's USB 3 half never appeared, with no error. The
pad setup for a USB 3 lane runs only when the lane's function is
"usb3-ss", upstream's name; R35 names that function "xusb" on Tegra210, as
R32's device trees do, so the setup never ran. The five checks now test for
the name the lanes carry. The register value is the same either way.

Tested on the Nano: in trial 30 the hub's USB 3 half (0bda:0411) came up at
SuperSpeed, as under 4.9.

Licence: GPL-2.0-only. Lab notes, with every measurement: NOTES.md.
---
diff --git a/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c b/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c
index 4792693..4ee3ffa 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c
@@ -736,7 +736,7 @@ static int tegra210_sata_uphy_enable(struct tegra_xusb_padctl *padctl)
 	if (tegra210_plle_hw_sequence_is_enabled())
 		goto skip_pll_init;
 
-	usb = tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "usb3-ss");
+	usb = tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "xusb");
 
 	err = clk_prepare_enable(sata->pll);
 	if (err < 0)
@@ -2847,7 +2847,13 @@ static int tegra210_pcie_phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 							tegra210_usb3_lane_map(lane));
 	}
 
-	if (tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "usb3-ss"))
+	/*
+	 * R35 names these lanes' USB3 function "xusb", as R32's device trees do
+	 * (tegra210_pcie_functions, tegra210_usb3_port_map()), where upstream
+	 * names it "usb3-ss". Checking for "usb3-ss" never matched, so the USB3
+	 * pad was never set up and no SuperSpeed device connected.
+	 */
+	if (tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "xusb"))
 		err = tegra210_usb3_phy_power_on(phy);
 
 	mutex_unlock(&padctl->lock);
@@ -2862,7 +2868,7 @@ static int tegra210_pcie_phy_power_off(struct phy *phy)
 
 	mutex_lock(&padctl->lock);
 
-	if (tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "usb3-ss"))
+	if (tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "xusb"))
 		err = tegra210_usb3_phy_power_off(phy);
 
 	mutex_unlock(&padctl->lock);
@@ -3031,7 +3037,7 @@ static int tegra210_sata_phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 				tegra210_usb3_lane_map(lane));
 	}
 
-	if (tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "usb3-ss"))
+	if (tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "xusb"))
 		err = tegra210_usb3_phy_power_on(phy);
 
 	mutex_unlock(&padctl->lock);
@@ -3046,7 +3052,7 @@ static int tegra210_sata_phy_power_off(struct phy *phy)
 
 	mutex_lock(&padctl->lock);
 
-	if (tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "usb3-ss"))
+	if (tegra_xusb_lane_check(lane, "xusb"))
 		err = tegra210_usb3_phy_power_off(phy);
 
 	mutex_unlock(&padctl->lock);
